sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Camera hack, for every site: a WebGL canvas that is drawn once while it
    is out of view (an on-demand renderer such as X_ITE) shows both eyes;
    the left eye is the page's own camera, so a 2D output shows exactly what
    the page draws; the zero-parallax plane follows the scene inside the
    person's popped limit, for the camera hack and for the flat WebXR
    display.
  * The camera hack's separation comes from the person's depth limits built
    on the display (kde_stereo_depth_v1 depth_limits) instead of a fixed 2
    percent of the width: a point at infinity lands at the sunk limit in the
    output's pixels whatever the canvas's width; the 3D Canvas menu's Less,
    Normal, More and Most stay the person's choice on top and scale it, never
    past the limit (webgl.stereo-camera.
    separation-from-limits off keeps the fixed percentage).
  * The browser has no setting for depth, the screen plane or the kind of
    device: the 3D Canvas and 3D Display menus' Less, Normal, More and Most,
    the screen plane choices and Flat TV, Flat headset and VR over the phone
    are gone, with their preferences and strings in the nine languages. The
    depth is the person's limits from KWin, unscaled; a Display Settings item
    opens KDE's Display Configuration, where they are changed (systemsettings kcm_kscreen). The per-site 3D on and off, the
    video's input packing and Swap Eyes stay.
  * No separation is made up: a 3D scene in a worker gets the limits the
    process was told, and a scene whose limits are not known stays flat, with
    a notice in the browser's notification bar where the desktop has no Stereo
    KWin. The Display Configuration label is KDE's own name for the page.
  * Spanish (es-ES, es-MX, es-AR, es-CL) for the edition's 3D menus and
    notices, and the four Spanish locales are in the package.
  * A depth buffer that cannot be read, so that the plane stays the
    camera's own, is said once on the page's web console, with the reason.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
